      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-10-26_WidnesExaminer_art0015" n="art0015">
        <head>BOVRIL.</head>
        <p>BOVRIL.</p>
        <p>FOR INVALIDS.</p>
        <p>Infinitely NOURISHING Than ordinary LT EXTRACT, or BEEF</p>
        <p>IMPROVEMENTS • IN THE CHEMICAL</p>
        <p>ID4 DUSTRY.</p>
        <p>The very large -circle of people who are interested in the chemical trade will shortly -have formal announce- ment made of a new process for the manufacture of caustic soda and :bleaching powder—two of the chief products of that industry—which amounts to a revolu- tion, and must produce great chauges in the conditions on which the manufacture is at present carried en. The new process is the invention of Mr. Hamilton G. Cost- ner, the American chemist, who brought cut the new process for the production of aluminium which was worked at Oldbury,near Birmingbam,by the Aluminium Company, which controls the new system referred to. Hitherto caustic soda and bleaching-powder, which are the chief precincts of the works in the United Alkalia Company or Chemical Union, hate been produced hv the old Leblanc process, Which 14 as old as the year 1791 but has been improved since from time to time. By this process, however, it is found difficult to produce caustic soda for less than £B, cr bleaching-powder for less than £5 10s, per ton., Castner's process reduces the cost of manufacturing caustic soda to £4 53. and of bleaching-powder to about £3 per ton,so that it is much more economical. But this is not all. The ordinary quality of caustic soda corresponds to what is known as 70 per cent. Liverpool test, whereas the soda produced by the Costner process sumer; to 78.5 per cent. Liver- -paol test, and is of almost chemical purity,which would, of co3rse, make it a deal more valnahle, even if it cost as much to produce. The fundamental feature of the Castner process is the ersployment of a moving body of mercury, which aids the electric action to form an amal- gam, which is decomposed electrically as soon as it is se formeci.The cells employed are different from any hither- to suggested, and only one-fifth of the size used in any other proeess, actual or proposed. The great cheapness of the new syatem is mainly due to the fact that it re- qnires very little labour, being for the most part auto- matic. The Aluminium Company have been working the_proeess experimentally at Oldbury for about a year and are now about to build large works to manufacture caustic and-bleach. in competition with the existing works engaged in tVse industrizs.</p>
