        <p>• THE STEEL CRISIS AT BARItOW tee : or The executive committee repr or esenting workers at Barrow, who are lock* d out on Vetio y, beer; ',Agee, have roplied to the overtures which r!aeueritis, made by the Mayor of Barrow and other ol't, the members of the county council with reference ,43 told restarting of the steel works. The men have ber4 the they can commence operations on the terTvg:oo, in° Jeremiah Head award plus five per cent take consequence of the improvement which has slnecogoise place in the trade. They will not, however, r ewes the Head award, becauqe, they say, in rnanY rie the' the wages paid to the workers are on a lower sctmi the obtsins elsewhers,but they are anxious to weir u_rre", and dise2tors with Mr. Traw, their general socrer!h'e hope then go into the whole question. They express 6iththe that the Mayor of Barrow and those moving wsince will endeavour to brina about this inte.rview• as „coo uP men were locked out the price of steel rails h El a ton, and the market is brisk with.orders.</p>
