        <p>Only eight election petitions have been filed after all, though to judge from the rumours which fly about after every General Election quite ten times that number might have been expected. Two of these concern metropolitan seats, and will be tried at the Law Courts. Mr.Willis,Q.C.,will appear both for Mr. Cremer (llaggerston) and Mr. J. William, Bean (St. George's-in-the-East), the petitioners. The other cases come from Lichfield, Lancaster Sunderland, and Southampton, and in the first only is the petitioner a Unionists. The Durham petition, we now learn, has been withdrawn.</p>
