      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-10-26_WidnesExaminer_art0039" n="art0039">
        <head>CHEERY HOME</head>
        <p>A CHEERY HOME</p>
        <p>at even-tide, is the molt comfortable hone in these shortening autumn days, Happy family, cosy fire- side-corner, puss purring on the hearth, kettle croon- ing on the hob and—realest treat of alt—Brooke Bonds' steaming cup that cheers and warms the cockles the heart—all here to prove there's no place like home</p>
        <p>IN 'CHILL OCTOBER.' Now this good Te that makes and cherishes so many happy homes,is within the easy reach of every- body, for Brooke Bonds Agents are everywhere, and for four or five-pence, they will gladly hand you a quarter-poun I p4cket, which will make enough to fill about forty cups Yes, how good is this Brooke, Bonds' Tea I Re- freshing, contenting, rest-giving, it's the daily com- forter of m re th Ln L million weary ones.</p>
