      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-10-26_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>IROOKE, BOND &amp; CO., LTII</head>
        <p>IROOKE, BOND &amp; CO., LTII</p>
        <p>THE LANCA,SIHRE TEA WAREHOUSES 17. PICCADILLY, 29. MARICET 6TREET MANCHESTE</p>
        <p>A fine of 53. with the option of three days' imprison- ment, has been passed by the Dormitory magistrates on the Hon. Mr. Feilding, brother to the Earl of Denbigh, for riding a bicycle without a light. Mr. Fei!ding de- clined to p.ty the fine, and expressing anxiety to" see the interibr of a Scotch prison," was conveyed to Craig- inches Gaol. Aberdeen, the C untess of Denbigh accom- panying Wm to Banchory Station. • TRIED AND PROVED.</p>
