        <p>HOW TO HELP THE CHESHIRE FARMER. If we could have the beautiful SWEET MILK Which is now used in Cheshire in making POOR UNSALEABLE CHEESE sent to a Creamery Where it could be made into FRESH CREAM BUTTER on the most approved scientific princi- Plea, it would open up a NEW INDUSTRY to which there would scarcely be ANY LIMIT if the light QUALITY was produced. It would greatly relieve the Market of the Class of CHEESE which DOES NOT PAY the Farmer to make,and those who have facilities and convenience to make FINN CHEESE would get a BETTER PRICE for them. To establish these Creameries up and down the County only means ENTERPRISE and CAPI- TAL and not so mach Capital as some would think. Such a CREAMERY has already been estab- lished in CHESN RE and BUTTER of the most DELICIOUS FLAVOUR and QUALITY is I.eing Made, and I have been asked tt take the Agency for the sale of it, which I gladly do, because if I get QUALITY I prefer to sell a ROME .MADE article to a FOREIGN. I shall sell ,at a SMALL PROFIT to induce trade and encourage the Enterprise. PRESENT PRICE FIFTEEN PENCE PER LB. Try a Sample Pound. J. B. ISAAC, PROVISION MERCHANT, WARRINGTON.</p>
